VVEERRSSIIOONNSS
       XSI requires that CCLLOOCCKKSS__PPEERR__SSEECC equals 1000000 independent of the
       actual resolution.

       On several other implementations, the value returned by cclloocckk() also
       includes the times of any children whose status has been collected via
       wwaaiitt(2) (or another wait‐type call).  Linux does not include the times
       of waited‐for children in the value returned by cclloocckk().  The ttiimmeess(2)
       function, which explicitly returns (separate) information about the
       caller and its children, may be preferable.

