HHIISSTTOORRYY
       POSIX.1‐2001, C89.

       In glibc 2.17 and earlier, cclloocckk() was implemented on top of ttiimmeess(2).
       For improved accuracy, since glibc 2.18, it is implemented on top of
       cclloocckk__ggeettttiimmee(2) (using the CCLLOOCCKK__PPRROOCCEESSSS__CCPPUUTTIIMMEE__IIDD clock).

NNOOTTEESS
       The C standard allows for arbitrary values at the start of the program;
       subtract the value returned from a call to cclloocckk() at the start of the
       program to get maximum portability.

       Note that the time can wrap around.  On a 32‐bit system where
       CCLLOOCCKKSS__PPEERR__SSEECC equals 1000000 this function will return the same value
       approximately every 72 minutes.

